Jonathan Ai scheduling is adapted from Octop's cron manager. Jobs are stored
in a local SQLite file, one file per user, and the default timezone is
America/Phoenix. A job is either a fixed text message or an agent task.
Agent tasks use the same tool approvals and shell guard as an interactive
chat. Missed runs inside a short grace window are caught up once; older
missed runs are skipped and written to the job log. Users can run a job
now, and enable, disable, or delete it. Jonathan Ai uses the Python stdlib
for storage and time zones. It does not add APScheduler, and it does not
call a third-party hosted endpoint.

