Jonathan Ai voice is adapted from Octop's voice manager: an active
speech-to-text provider, an active text-to-speech provider, and a single
place that dispatches a recording or a spoken reply. Jonathan Ai does not
vendor Octop's browser, Edge, Tencent, or MiMo presets. The default
speech-to-text engine is local faster-whisper and the default voice is
local Piper. OpenAI and xAI are optional and run only after they are
selected. Microphones and speakers, including Bluetooth headsets, are
chosen from the Windows WASAPI devices or the Linux PulseAudio and
PipeWire devices. Push-to-talk is the default. The wake word is off until
the user turns it on, and that check stays on this machine. Model files
are fetched from Hugging Face or the official Piper and Whisper sources
and checked with SHA-256. The optional install extra is voice
(pip install "clawd-codex[voice]").

