Jonathan Ai document search is adapted from Octop's knowledge base. PDF,
DOCX, Markdown, plain text, and HTML are split into passages and stored in
a per-user SQLite file under the user's home directory. Answers cite the
file name and the passage. Local embeddings use fastembed with the ONNX
build of BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5 from Hugging Face, and each file is checked
against a pinned checksum before it is used. Hosts other than huggingface.co
are refused. When that model is not on the machine, search uses BM25 and
still cites the file and passage. Document text stays on this machine unless
the user selects the OpenAI embedding provider. Jonathan Ai does not vendor
Octop's OCR, spreadsheet parsers, or its download race against other hosts.

