Jonathan Ai can hand a coding task to a local ACP runner. The client follows
Octop's outbound ACP runner: newline JSON-RPC on the runner's stdio, a
session in a chosen project folder, streamed session updates, and a list of
files that changed. Built-in runners are OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, and
Zed. Each stays disabled until the user enables it and sets a local program
path. Jonathan Ai does not download a runner and does not use npx. The
runner command and the project folder go through the approval gate, and the
shell guard still holds a dangerous command. A permission request from the
runner is cancelled until the user approves it here. The protocol itself
stays on this machine.

