Jonathan Ai chat channels and LAN device control follow Octop's gateway:
one inbound message is normalized, checked against an allow-list, and
answered on the same channel. Jonathan Ai implements Telegram, Discord,
and Slack only. Bot tokens are stored in the OS keyring when it is
available, otherwise in an encrypted file on this machine, and they are
not written into settings or logs. Device control is limited to MQTT,
Home Assistant REST, generic HTTP, and SSH targets the user registers.
Discovery reads the ARP table and can send one mDNS query and one SSDP
search. Every device action asks for approval, and each device has its
own allow-list of actions. Only loopback, private, and link-local
addresses are accepted. Jonathan Ai does not include the upstream
channels for other regions, does not import the octop-gateway package,
and does not call a third-party host for the protocol itself.

